# 2FA setup checklist (frontend)

> Generated by `auth:setup`. Do these steps, tick them, then delete this file. How 2FA works: https://github.com/Light-it-labs/lightit-auth-laravel/blob/main/docs/google-2fa.md

- [ ] **Install dependencies** (`{{ packageManager }}`): {{ dependencyReport }}
- [ ] **Use the 2FA-aware login hook** in `src/routes/(public)/_guest/login/-components/login-form.tsx`:
  1. Remove `import { useLogin } from "@/services/auth/actions";`
  2. Add `import { useTwoFactorLogin } from "../-hooks/use-two-factor-login";` after the `"@/utils"` import
  3. Replace `const loginMutation = useLogin();` with `const loginMutation = useTwoFactorLogin();`
- [ ] **Add the i18n keys** to `src/i18n/locales/en.json` (and translate them in `es.json`): `form.otp` and
  `form.recoveryCode`, the `twoFactor` block and `navigation.links.twoFactor`. Copy them from **i18n keys to paste** below.
- [ ] **Link the account page from the sidebar** in `src/routes/_private/-components/sidebar/sidebar.tsx`, at the end of `links`:
  `{ path: "/account/two-factor", label: t("navigation.links.twoFactor"), icon: <Icons.Lock /> },`

Check it worked: run `vite` once (`dev` or `build`) so the router adds the 2FA routes, then
`{{ packageManager }} exec tsc --noEmit` passes, signing in with a 2FA user asks for the code, and **Two-factor** shows in the sidebar.

<details>
